{"algorithm":"ML-KEM","schema":"mlkem_test_schema.json","numberOfTests":202,"notes":{"Strcmp":{"bugType":"CAN_OF_WORMS","description":"In ML-KEM.Decaps the ciphertext is compared with the output of K-PKE.Encrypt for implicit rejection. If an implementation were to use strcmp() for that comparison it would fail to reject some ciphertexts if a zero byte terminates the comparison early. The chance of it occurring randomly is 2⁻¹⁶. These vectors are valid and test that the implicit rejection path is taken as expected."},"MalleableCiphertext":{"bugType":"CAN_OF_WORMS","description":"The ciphertext is malleable."}},"testGroups":[{"type":"MLKEMTest","source":{"name":"CCTV/strcmp","version":"0.1"},"parameterSet":"ML-KEM-1024","tests":[{"tcId":1,"flags":["Strcmp"],"seed":"8247c17686a8bc0b3afebe6bed1df1dc3ff7fa07c3670f624930235f20aecb4353ece11faa61f47d946ee501abb9a48029096de63b243a1794c4a760f98cc157","ek":"","c":"","K":"c6338bf92f3930b95f81d87fe669fabc42aaa549e8fecfbfdbe237d739fe4d96","result":"valid"}]},{"type":"MLKEMTest","source":{"name":"FIPS 203","version":"1.0"},"parameterSet":"ML-KEM-1024","tests":[{"tcId":2,"comment":"Test vector based on official round 3 seeds 0","flags":[],"seed":"7c9935a0b07694aa0c6d10e4db6b1add2fd81a25ccb148032dcd739936737f2d8626ed79d451140800e03b59b956f8210e556067407d13dc90fa9e8b872bfb8f","ek":"","c":"","K":"489dd1e9c2be4af3482bdb35bb26ce760e6e414da6ecbe489985748a825f1cd6","result":"valid"},{"tcId":102,"comment":"Private key too short","flags":[],"seed":"ed9e26756bf76b589087763e6129a06fb95da14f01fa7dc6863996caf8d1f22cd41b5b35197ebf41d2d97f2ce8a3f973d4be0f47","c":"","K":"","result":"invalid"}]},{"type":"MLKEMTest","source":{"name":"github.com/007bsd/mlkem-implicit-rejection","version":"1"},"parameterSet":"ML-KEM-1024","tests":[{"tcId":194,"comment":"Ciphertext modified at byte 0 (c1 poly-block 0); implicit rejection must fire, so a re-encryption comparison that skips this position is detected","flags":["MalleableCiphertext"],"seed":"7c9935a0b07694